{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786606709199,"sessionID":"ses_005f19fdfffeOBUKa90a14PLKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_SG4ML6drJMqCJf9lgx6M8488","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/timeline.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/timeline.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # timeline.md — Reference Design (ds-a research deliverable)\n2: \n3: > Design artifact produced by the ds-a fan-out research lineage. This is the PROPOSED schema/placement for the real `timeline.md` that must be generated and committed at `specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/timeline.md` BEFORE any consolidation rename executes. This file documents the design; it is not yet the canonical timeline.\n4: \n5: ## Purpose\n6: Record the true chronological order in which each 036 spec folder was created and worked, keyed by a stable identity that is NOT the folder number, so the lineage survives any renumbering.\n7: \n8: ## Canonical location\n9: - Root: `specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/timeline.md`\n10: - After consolidation: one scoped `timeline.md` per group parent; root remains canonical.\n11: \n12: ## Schema\n13: ```markdown\n14: # Timeline — 036-deep-loop-innovation (chronological lineage record)\n15: > Immutable identity record. Do NOT reorder rows; append only.\n16: > Renumbering folders MUST NOT change chrono_id / worked_order / created timestamps.\n17: \n18: | chrono_id | folder_slug | band | created_at | git_first_add | last_save_at | status | worked_order |\n19: |-----------|-------------|------|------------|---------------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n20: | T001      | 001-deep-loop-market-research | 000-foundation-and-planning | 2026-07-15T19:00:45Z | 2026-07-14T22:32:08+02:00 | 2026-07-17T13:31:05Z | complete | 1 |\n21: ```\n22: \n23: ## Rules\n24: 1. `chrono_id` (T001, T002, …) is the stable key, assigned once in original git-first-add order (tie-break by folder number for the 07-15/16 planning batch).\n25: 2. `worked_order` is the derived execution sequence: git_first_add primary → created_at tie-break → last_save_at final tie-break; `notes` column records anomalies (planning batch, remediation rework).\n26: 3. `band` records the post-consolidation group parent so the timeline doubles as the old→new mapping.\n27: 4. Append-only: new children get the next chrono_id at the end; never reorder rows. A rename updates only `folder_slug`/`band`, never chrono_id/worked_order/timestamps.\n28: 5. Generated once from `git log --all --follow --diff-filter=A` + child `graph-metadata.json`, then reviewed and committed before any rename.\n29: \n30: ## Derived worked order (all 44 children)\n31: 1. 001 (git 2026-07-14) — truly first\n32: 2. 002→017 planning batch (07-15/16, by folder number)\n33: 3. 018 (07-19/20)\n34: 4. 050 (07-27) — authored early despite 05x number\n35: 5. 019, 020 (07-29)\n36: 6. 022→032 (07-31, by folder number)\n37: 7. 021 (created 07-30, first commit 08-03)\n38: 8. 033 (08-05/08-08)\n39: 9. 035 (08-07)\n40: 10. 047, 048, 049 (08-08)\n41: 11. 051 (08-12)\n42: 12. 052 (08-12)\n43: 13. 053, 054, 055, 056 (08-13)\n44: \n45: ## Why this survives renumbering\n46: The current numbering already diverges from work order: 050 worked before 019/020; 021 after 022-032; 047-049 after 033. Without this record, a renumber irretrievably loses that order.\n\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# timeline.md — Reference Design (ds-a research deliverable)\n\n> Design artifact produced by the ds-a fan-out research lineage. This is the PROPOSED schema/placement for the real `timeline.md` that must be generated and committed at `specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/timeline.md` BEFORE any consolidation rename executes. This file documents the design; it is not yet the canonical timeline.\n\n## Purpose\nRecord the true chronological order in which each 036 spec folder was created and worked, keyed by a stable identity that is NOT the folder number, so the lineage survives any renumbering.\n\n## Canonical location\n- Root: `specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/timeline.md`\n- After consolidation: one scoped `timeline.md` per group parent; root remains canonical.\n\n## Schema\n```markdown\n# Timeline — 036-deep-loop-innovation (chronological lineage record)\n> Immutable identity record. Do NOT reorder rows; append only.\n> Renumbering folders MUST NOT change chrono_id / worked_order / created timestamps.\n\n| chrono_id | folder_slug | band | created_at | git_first_add | last_save_at | status | worked_order |\n|-----------|-------------|------|------------|---------------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| T001      | 001-deep-loop-market-research | 000-foundation-and-planning | 2026-07-15T19:00:45Z | 2026-07-14T22:32:08+02:00 | 2026-07-17T13:31:05Z | complete | 1 |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/timeline.md","text":"# timeline.md — Reference Design (ds-a research deliverable)\n\n> Design artifact produced by the ds-a fan-out research lineage. This is the PROPOSED schema/placement for the real `timeline.md` that must be generated and committed at `specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/timeline.md` BEFORE any consolidation rename executes. This file documents the design; it is not yet the canonical timeline.\n\n## Purpose\nRecord the true chronological order in which each 036 spec folder was created and worked, keyed by a stable identity that is NOT the folder number, so the lineage survives any renumbering.\n\n## Canonical location\n- Root: `specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/timeline.md`\n- After consolidation: one scoped `timeline.md` per group parent; root remains canonical.\n\n## Schema\n```markdown\n# Timeline — 036-deep-loop-innovation (chronological lineage record)\n> Immutable identity record. Do NOT reorder rows; append only.\n> Renumbering folders MUST NOT change chrono_id / worked_order / created timestamps.\n\n| chrono_id | folder_slug | band | created_at | git_first_add | last_save_at | status | worked_order |\n|-----------|-------------|------|------------|---------------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| T001      | 001-deep-loop-market-research | 000-foundation-and-planning | 2026-07-15T19:00:45Z | 2026-07-14T22:32:08+02:00 | 2026-07-17T13:31:05Z | complete | 1 |\n```\n\n## Rules\n1. `chrono_id` (T001, T002, …) is the stable key, assigned once in original git-first-add order (tie-break by folder number for the 07-15/16 planning batch).\n2. `worked_order` is the derived execution sequence: git_first_add primary → created_at tie-break → last_save_at final tie-break; `notes` column records anomalies (planning batch, remediation rework).\n3. `band` records the post-consolidation group parent so the timeline doubles as the old→new mapping.\n4. Append-only: new children get the next chrono_id at the end; never reorder rows. A rename updates only `folder_slug`/`band`, never chrono_id/worked_order/timestamps.\n5. Generated once from `git log --all --follow --diff-filter=A` + child `graph-metadata.json`, then reviewed and committed before any rename.\n\n## Derived worked order (all 44 children)\n1. 001 (git 2026-07-14) — truly first\n2. 002→017 planning batch (07-15/16, by folder number)\n3. 018 (07-19/20)\n4. 050 (07-27) — authored early despite 05x number\n5. 019, 020 (07-29)\n6. 022→032 (07-31, by folder number)\n7. 021 (created 07-30, first commit 08-03)\n8. 033 (08-05/08-08)\n9. 035 (08-07)\n10. 047, 048, 049 (08-08)\n11. 051 (08-12)\n12. 052 (08-12)\n13. 053, 054, 055, 056 (08-13)\n\n## Why this survives renumbering\nThe current numbering already diverges from work order: 050 worked before 019/020; 021 after 022-032; 047-049 after 033. Without this record, a renumber irretrievably loses that order.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":46,"totalLines":46,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/timeline.md","time":{"start":1786606709192,"end":1786606709197}},"id":"prt_ffa0ee348001ZHFsTNaPM6xom6","sessionID":"ses_005f19fdfffeOBUKa90a14PLKH","messageID":"msg_ffa0ea3cf001nMznfrKu1nxrQc"}}
